        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "This was the behavior up until ada2007453 (\"feat(dir): provider framework #40738\"), and is also the behavior of all other similar plugins I know of. I should maybe have mentioned this in the commit. I assumed it was an unintentional regression.\r\n\r\nI can still of course open an issue for discussion, but I honestly cannot see how the current behavior is more intuitive: if I'm in `$PWD` and I open the directory lister, I would expect to see `$PWD`, not `$PWD/..`.",
